detail.body:
Closes the first implementation checkpoint of #494 when the required evidence is green.

## What changed

- added an additive editorial composition layer for the public site;
- added typed editorial primitives for large display fields, technical rails, critical state pairs and route transitions;
- recomposed PUB-001 around the existing governed product truth instead of adding new claims;
- kept `.arq opens` adjacent to `does not save back` as a first-class visual state pair;
- widened the public shell while leaving the existing static/reference baseline intact;
- copied `design/tokens/brand.v4.css` directly into the generated site and bridged marketing accent use to canonical brand tokens;
- removed the stale hard-coded `2026-08` revision month from the footer;
- preserved the no-client-JS and no-third-party-resource architecture.

## Authority and ownership

- integration authority resolved through #332;
- branch created from exact integration head `df04288c182bdfcee91f92e70b0e5d0017fc0628`;
- implementation branch: `codex/arq-public-site-editorial-v1`;
- owned slice recorded in #494.

## Deliberate limits

- no merge requested yet;
- no claim that the page is visually approved until screenshot/human review exists;
- no fake product screenshot was added. The hero uses an explicitly decorative abstract semantic-plan graphic;
- no PUB-002+ rollout in this PR yet;
- the separate anti-slop file mentioned by the owner has not been supplied, so no assumptions from it are encoded.

## Evidence needed

CI must establish build/type/test/language/claim invariants on this exact head. Visual and 200% zoom evidence still requires a browser-capable execution pass before this is ready to merge.

Related: #205, #332, #369, #377, #494
